messages.content:
Generate a standalone C reproducer that triggers this vulnerability:

File: libtiff/tif_next.c
Line: 79
Function: NeXTDecode
Bug type: divide-by-zero
CWE: CWE-369
Explanation: scanline is taken from tif->tif_scanlinesize and can be 0 (e.g., if scanline size computation overflowed and was clamped to 0 by the core library). The code performs occ % scanline without checking for zero, causing a divide-by-zero crash before any further validation.

Source context:
```c
